2,Manat - Languages - Fieldwork - Don Daniels,https://dondaniels.weebly.com/manat.html,"Manat is spoken by about fifty people in two villages, Paynamar and Simbevi. All its speakers are over forty years old, making the language highly endangered. Children are learning Tok Pisin instead. Manat belongs to the Sogeram family, which is part of the Madang branch of the Trans New Guinea family. I first met some Manat speakers in 2006, in the Nend-speaking village of Akavanku. I did ...",Manat,Trans-New Guinea
